From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 10:33:25 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Link vetted secret cleansing in V2 signing consumers

Use the existing crypto target in the full validation library and compile support/cleanse.cpp in standalone consumers, with its source include path. Release VM test and runner build and the VM suite pass. The independently owned development-chain test dependency follows with indexed initializer tests.
---
 src/lotus_v2/CMakeLists.txt                   |  2 +-
 src/lotus_v2/block_test/CMakeLists.txt        | 17 +++++++++--------
 src/lotus_v2/disk_block_test/CMakeLists.txt   |  3 ++-
 src/lotus_v2/ordinary_test/CMakeLists.txt     |  3 ++-
 src/lotus_v2/peer_codec_test/CMakeLists.txt   |  3 ++-
 src/lotus_v2/peer_session_test/CMakeLists.txt |  3 ++-
 src/lotus_v2/vm_test/CMakeLists.txt           |  5 +++--
 7 files changed, 21 insertions(+), 15 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/lotus_v2/CMakeLists.txt b/src/lotus_v2/CMakeLists.txt
index c22785a4d..999bdda18 100644
--- a/src/lotus_v2/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/lotus_v2/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -136,7 +136,7 @@ add_library(lotus_v2_validation STATIC
     monetary.cpp block_wire.cpp block_cost.cpp header_context.cpp
     asert_candidate.cpp block_transition.cpp disk_state.cpp disk_block.cpp development_chain.cpp disk_body.cpp)
 target_link_libraries(lotus_v2_validation PUBLIC
-    lotus_v2_sparse_state lotus_v2_incremental_utxo Boost::headers secp256k1 leveldb OpenSSL::Crypto)
+    lotus_v2_sparse_state lotus_v2_incremental_utxo Boost::headers secp256k1 leveldb OpenSSL::Crypto crypto)
 
 # Compare the disk path against the retained in-memory connector oracle using
 # the same dependencies selected by the full daemon build.
